1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:05,260
Robbie, this new Walkman is absolutely wonderful.

2
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:09,270
Richard and Marilyn bought it for me for my birthday.

3
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:11,460
They're so thoughtful.

4
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:16,670
You are very lucky, Robbie, to have such a nice family.

5
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:18,740
Is something wrong, Alexandra?

6
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:21,110
No, nothing.

7
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:22,550
Yes, there is.

8
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:24,690
I can tell.

9
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:26,770
What's the matter?

10
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:29,340
Come on, you can tell me.

11
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:31,010
What's up?

12
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:33,340
I don't know.

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,340
Something's wrong.

14
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:42,530
OK, let's talk.

15
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:46,370
I received a letter from my parents this morning.

16
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:48,400
Did they write some bad news?

17
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,320
No.

18
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:52,420
Well, then why are you so sad?

19
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,050
I miss them.

20
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:56,750
I miss them very much.

21
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:59,710
I'm sorry, Alexandra.

22
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:03,980
But I understand.

23
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,420
The Molinas treat me so nicely,

24
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:11,750
and I love being with your family so much ...

25
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:13,320
but when I received the letter

26
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:17,420
with photographs of my family, I cried.

27
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:19,960
I cried because I miss them all.

28
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,990
You really miss your family, don't you?

29
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:27,430
Yes. I know I must seem silly.

30
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:30,140
It's not like I have nobody.

31
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:32,300
I like the Molinas very much,

32
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:39,250
and they're so kind to me.

33
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:40,790
Hey, why don't we go out

34
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:42,590
for a cheeseburger and french fries?

35
00:01:42,590 --> 00:01:44,560
That'll cheer you up.

36
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,730
And you can use my Walkman.

37
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:50,490
That's a good idea.

38
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:52,630
But if we go out,

39
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:55,710
please don't complain

40
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:58,680
about your math teacher or your math homework.

41
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,990
I want to have fun.

42
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:01,770
So do I.

43
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:03,130
I have to turn off the lights,

44
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:05,810
or else my father will get really angry.

45
00:02:05,810 --> 00:02:09,240
He says I never turn them out when I leave.

46
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:14,980
If they come home and they're on ...

47
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:16,310
Do you hear something?

48
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:16,730
Yes.

49
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:19,190
What was that?

50
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:21,890
It sounded like a dog barking.

51
00:02:21,890 --> 00:02:24,270
It sounded like a dog barking right here.

52
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:28,510
Yeah.

53
00:02:28,510 --> 00:02:29,660
A dog!

54
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:33,690
A springer spaniel!

55
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:34,330
Come on in!

56
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:36,170
Make yourself at home.

57
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:39,810
Oh, you poor little thing.

58
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:49,050
Come on.

59
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:51,260
Poor baby.

60
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:57,040
Where did you come from?

61
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,740
Her name's Gemma,

62
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:02,150
and she belongs to Mr. and Mrs. Levinson.

63
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:04,250
There's a phone number --

64
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:09,400
five five five ... eight four four eight.

65
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,740
Robbie, maybe you should call them

66
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:15,130
and tell the Levinsons we have their cute little spaniel.

67
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:17,110
I've always wanted a springer spaniel.

68
00:03:17,110 --> 00:03:35,820
She's so cute.

69
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:42,110
The number you are calling -- 555-8448 --

70
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:46,900
is no longer in service.

71
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:51,490
The number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:51,490 --> 00:03:54,080
Oh, you poor, poor baby.

73
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,400
You've lost your family.

74
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,210
We'll find them.

75
00:03:57,210 --> 00:04:00,210
Don't worry, Alexandra.
